  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe object being ignored is marked with を. Very commonly used in daily conversation and writing. Can describe both deliberate ignoring of a person (giving the silent treatment) and disregarding rules or advice.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {信号|しんごう}を{無視|むし}する (run a traffic light)\n- {忠告|ちゅうこく}を{無視|むし}する (ignore advice)\n- {意見|いけん}を{無視|むし}する (disregard someone's opinion)\n- {完全|かんぜん}に{無視|むし}する (completely ignore)\n- {存在|そんざい}を{無視|むし}する (ignore someone's existence)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {無視|むし}: the noun form, also very common ({無視|むし}される 'to be ignored')\n- {見|み}て{見|み}ぬふりをする: to pretend not to see — implies awareness but choosing not to act\n- {放|ほう}っておく: to leave alone — less deliberate; can mean simply not dealing with something",
